@startuml 11_Send_Message

title 11. When Message Is Sent

actor User
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "Memory Cache" as Memory
participant "Crypto Layer" as Crypto
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "Database" as DB
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Other Members" as Recipients

User -> Client: Type message and send
activate Client

Client -> Memory: Get latest token
activate Memory
note right of Memory
  Latest token already loaded
  when conversation was entered
end note
Memory --> Client: token (plaintext)
deactivate Memory

Client -> Crypto: Encrypt message
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  encrypted_content = Encrypt(
    message_plaintext,
    token
  )
  
  Using AES-256-GCM
  Includes nonce for uniqueness
end note
Crypto --> Client: encrypted_content
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Server: POST /messages\n{conv_id, encrypted_content, token_version: "v_1.3.5"}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Validate:\n- User is member\n- Token version exists\n- Not banned

Server -> DB: INSERT message\n{encrypted_content, token_version, sender_id, timestamp}
activate DB
note right of DB
  Server stores encrypted content
  Cannot decrypt (needs token)
end note
DB --> Server: Message ID
deactivate DB

Server -> WS: Broadcast to conversation members
activate WS
note right of WS
  Real-time delivery
  to online members
end note
WS -> Recipients: New message notification\n{message_id, encrypted_content, token_version}
deactivate WS

Server --> Client: 201 Created\n{message_id, timestamp}
deactivate Server

Client -> Memory: Store plaintext in memory cache
activate Memory
note right of Memory
  Cache decrypted message
  for instant display
  (memory only, not persistent)
end note
Memory --> Client: Cached
deactivate Memory

Client --> User: Message sent ✓
deactivate Client

note over User, Recipients
  E2EE properties:
  ✅ Message encrypted client-side
  ✅ Server only sees ciphertext
  ✅ Only members with token can decrypt
  ✅ Real-time delivery via WebSocket
  🔐 Server cannot read message content
end note

@enduml
